{"id":"feature-map","name":"Feature map","description":"Story / feature map: stages, steps and features per increment","tags":["feature map","story map","agile","release","miro"],"source":"samples/3.png","doc":{"id":"tpl","name":"Feature map","page":{"w":1080,"h":480,"background":"#fefefe","pattern":null},"elements":[{"id":"e2s","kind":"rect","x":206,"y":40,"w":186,"h":440,"params":{},"style":{"fill":"#ffffff","stroke":"none"},"text":{}},{"id":"e2t","kind":"rect","x":391,"y":128,"w":492,"h":151,"params":{},"style":{"fill":"#e7e7e7","stroke":"none"},"text":{}},{"id":"e2u","kind":"rect","x":391,"y":354,"w":492,"h":114,"params":{},"style":{"fill":"#e7e7e7","stroke":"none"},"text":{}},{"id":"e2v","kind":"text","x":206,"y":56,"w":180,"h":20,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"Feature map","align":"left","valign":"middle","font":"Inter","size":15.5,"weight":800,"color":"#111111"}},{"id":"e2w","kind":"rect","x":206,"y":77,"w":117,"h":10,"params":{},"style":{"fill":"#fe6204","stroke":"none"},"text":{"content":"How to use this template","font":"Inter","size":7.6,"weight":500,"color":"#ffffff","align":"left","pad":1}},{"id":"e2x","kind":"text","x":208,"y":106,"w":112,"h":170,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"**Why to use this template?**\n*Identify or summarise steps, best practise and resulting features (epics / stories) so that you can define a narrative-complete solution in line with identified outcomes.*\n\nFeature maps (or Story maps) are our default tool to elicit and visualise features and scope at overview and detailed level. A Featuremap is based on an end-to-end process (user journey) that provides value to a user and assigns features, epics or stories that enable each step of the journey in priority order.\n\nThe teams we work with use Feature maps as the key tools to define, prioritise and communicate scope.\n\n**How to do it:**\n\n1. AGREE TARGET AUDIENCE AND THEIR GOALS\n2. MAP OVERALL JOURNEY\n3. IDENTIFY AND MAP FEATURES AGAINST THE JOURNEY\n4. DEFINE RELEASES\n5. ASSIGN FEATURES TO RELEASES\n6. PRIORITISE ITEMS WITHIN RELEASE (optional)\n\n**Ultimately this is all about building meaningful features and prioritisation against release.**","align":"left","valign":"top","font":"Inter","size":4.2,"color":"#333333","lineHeight":1.35}},{"id":"e2y","kind":"rect","x":208,"y":430,"w":184,"h":49,"params":{},"style":{"fill":"#fe6204","stroke":"none"},"text":{}},{"id":"e2z","kind":"text","x":211,"y":433,"w":80,"h":12,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"**Template**\nContent model","align":"left","valign":"top","font":"Inter","size":3.8,"color":"#ffffff","lineHeight":1.35}},{"id":"e30","kind":"text","x":391,"y":134,"w":14,"h":26,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"Inc1","align":"center","valign":"middle","font":"Inter","size":9,"weight":800,"color":"#111111","vertical":true}},{"id":"e31","kind":"text","x":400,"y":156,"w":36,"h":10,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"Increment / Release\ndescription","align":"left","valign":"top","font":"Inter","size":2.6,"color":"#555555","lineHeight":1.35}},{"id":"e32","kind":"text","x":391,"y":286,"w":14,"h":26,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"Inc2","align":"center","valign":"middle","font":"Inter","size":9,"weight":800,"color":"#111111","vertical":true}},{"id":"e33","kind":"text","x":400,"y":308,"w":36,"h":10,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"Increment / Release\ndescription","align":"left","valign":"top","font":"Inter","size":2.6,"color":"#555555","lineHeight":1.35}},{"id":"e34","kind":"text","x":391,"y":360,"w":14,"h":26,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"Inc3","align":"center","valign":"middle","font":"Inter","size":9,"weight":800,"color":"#111111","vertical":true}},{"id":"e35","kind":"text","x":400,"y":382,"w":36,"h":10,"params":{},"style":{},"text":{"content":"Increment / Release\ndescription","align":"left","valign":"top","font":"Inter","size":2.6,"color":"#555555","lineHeight":1.35}},{"id":"e36","kind":"rect","x":438,"y":66,"w":37,"h":